From 4bc61043136a11d3fdea34424381ec96af149d85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ebben Aries <exa@dscp.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:22:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add <mouse><screenEdgeWarpTime> to switch workspace by
 dragging to edge

Like Openbox, holding a dragged window at the outer left/right edge of
the output layout for <screenEdgeWarpTime> ms switches to the adjacent
workspace, and the window comes along (workspaces_switch_to() already
moves the grabbed view). While held, it keeps switching at that
interval. <screenEdgeWarpMouse> optionally warps the cursor and window
to the opposite edge after each switch.

Outer left/right edges are reserved for warping when enabled, so they
no longer trigger snap-to-edge. Disabled by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
